    \\186\ACK\n\
    \\EOT\ACK\NUL\STX\SOH\DC2\ACK\135\SOH\STX\137\SOH\ETX\SUB\169\ACK Wait for an execution operation to complete. When the client initially\n\
    \ makes the request, the server immediately responds with the current status\n\
    \ of the execution. The server will leave the request stream open until the\n\
    \ operation completes, and then respond with the completed operation. The\n\
    \ server MAY choose to stream additional updates as execution progresses,\n\
    \ such as to provide an update as to the state of the execution.\n\
    \\n\
    \ In addition to the cases described for Execute, the WaitExecution method\n\
    \ may fail as follows:\n\
    \\n\
    \ * `NOT_FOUND`: The operation no longer exists due to any of a transient\n\
    \   condition, an unknown operation name, or if the server implements the\n\
    \   Operations API DeleteOperation method and it was called for the current\n\
    \   execution. The client should call `Execute` to retry.\n\
    \\n\
