    \\EOT\ACK\STX\STX\EOT\DC2\ACK\242\ETX\STX\244\ETX\ETX\SUB\157\NAK SplitBlob retrieves information about how a blob is split into chunks.\n\
    \\n\
    \ This call returns information about how a blob is split into chunks, and\n\
    \ returns a list of the chunk digests. Using the returned list of chunk digests,\n\
    \ a client can check which chunks are locally available and only fetch the\n\
    \ missing ones. The desired blob can be assembled by concatenating the fetched\n\
    \ chunks in the order of the digests in the list. The chunks SHOULD all be\n\
    \ available in the CAS.\n\
    \\n\
    \ This API can be used to reduce the required data to download a large blob\n\
    \ from CAS if some chunks from similar blobs are locally available. For this\n\
    \ procedure to work properly, blobs SHOULD be split in a content-defined way,\n\
    \ rather than with fixed-sized chunking.\n\
    \\n\
    \ If a split request is answered successfully, a client can expect the\n\
    \ following guarantees from the server:\n\
    \  1. The blob chunks are stored in CAS.\n\
    \  2. Concatenating the blob chunks in the order of the digest list returned\n\
    \     by the server results in the original blob.\n\
    \\n\
    \ Servers which implement this functionality MUST declare that they support\n\
    \ it by setting the\n\
    \ [CacheCapabilities.split_blob_support][build.bazel.remote.execution.v2.CacheCapabilities.split_blob_support]\n\
    \ field accordingly.\n\
    \\n\
    \ Clients MUST check that the server supports this capability, before using\n\
    \ it.\n\
    \\n\
    \ Clients SHOULD verify that the digest of the blob assembled by the fetched\n\
    \ chunks is equal to the requested blob digest.\n\
    \\n\
    \ The lifetimes of the generated chunk blobs MAY be independent of the\n\
    \ lifetime of the original blob. In particular:\n\
    \  * A blob and any chunk derived from it MAY be evicted from the CAS at\n\
    \    different times.\n\
    \  * A call to [SplitBlob][build.bazel.remote.execution.v2.ContentAddressableStorage.SplitBlob]\n\
    \    extends the lifetime of the original blob, and sets the lifetimes of\n\
    \    the resulting chunks (or extends the lifetimes of already-existing\n\
    \    chunks).\n\
    \  * Touching a chunk extends its lifetime, but the server MAY choose not\n\
    \    to extend the lifetime of the original blob.\n\
    \  * Touching the original blob extends its lifetime, but the server MAY\n\
    \    choose not to extend the lifetimes of chunks derived from it.\n\
    \\n\
    \ When blob splitting and splicing is used at the same time, the clients and\n\
    \ the server SHOULD agree out-of-band upon a chunking algorithm used by both\n\
    \ parties to benefit from each other's chunk data and avoid unnecessary data\n\
    \ duplication.\n\
    \\n\
    \ Errors:\n\
    \\n\
    \ * `NOT_FOUND`: The requested blob is not present in the CAS, OR there is no\n\
    \   split information available for the blob, OR at least one chunk needed to\n\
    \   reconstruct the blob is missing from the CAS.\n\
    \ * `RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED`: There is insufficient disk quota to store the blob\n\
    \   chunks.\n\
    \\n\
