    \\EOT\ACK\STX\STX\ENQ\DC2\ACK\173\EOT\STX\175\EOT\ETX\SUB\180\SYN SpliceBlob tells the CAS how chunks can compose a blob.\n\
    \\n\
    \ This is the complementary operation to the\n\
    \ [ContentAddressableStorage.SplitBlob][build.bazel.remote.execution.v2.ContentAddressableStorage.SplitBlob]\n\
    \ function to handle the chunked upload of large blobs to save upload\n\
    \ traffic.\n\
    \\n\
    \ When uploading a large blob using chunked upload, clients MUST first upload\n\
    \ all chunks to the CAS, then call this RPC to tell the server how those chunks\n\
    \ compose the original blob. The chunks referenced in the SpliceBlob call SHOULD be\n\
    \ available in the CAS before calling this RPC.\n\
    \\n\
    \ If a client needs to upload a large blob and is able to split a blob into\n\
    \ chunks in such a way that reusable chunks are obtained, e.g., by means of\n\
    \ content-defined chunking, it can first determine which parts of the blob\n\
    \ are already available in the remote CAS and upload the missing chunks, and\n\
    \ then use this API to store information on how the chunks compose the\n\
    \ original blob.\n\
    \\n\
    \ Servers which implement this functionality MUST declare that they support\n\
    \ it by setting the\n\
    \ [CacheCapabilities.splice_blob_support][build.bazel.remote.execution.v2.CacheCapabilities.splice_blob_support]\n\
    \ field accordingly.\n\
    \\n\
    \ Clients MUST check that the server supports this capability, before using\n\
    \ it.\n\
    \\n\
    \ In order to ensure data consistency of the CAS, the server MUST only add\n\
    \ blobs to the CAS after verifying their digests. In particular, servers MUST NOT\n\
    \ trust digests provided by the client. The server MAY accept a request as no-op\n\
    \ if the client-specified blob is already in CAS or if information on how to\n\
    \ construct the blob from chunks is available. If the client-specified blob is\n\
    \ not already in the CAS, the server MUST verify that the digest of the newly\n\
    \ created blob assembled from chunks matches the digest specified by the\n\
    \ client, and reject the request if they differ. Servers MAY choose to allow\n\
    \ overwriting existing chunk mappings or to store multiple chunk mappings for\n\
    \ the same blob.\n\
    \\n\
    \ When blob splitting and splicing is used at the same time, the clients and\n\
    \ the server SHOULD agree out-of-band upon a chunking algorithm used by both\n\
    \ parties to benefit from each other's chunk data and avoid unnecessary data\n\
    \ duplication.\n\
    \\n\
    \ Errors:\n\
