    \\EOT\EOT\SOH\STX\NUL\DC2\EOT\196\ENQ\STX \SUB\193\ACK The arguments to the command.\n\
    \\n\
    \ The first argument specifies the command to run, which may be either an\n\
    \ absolute path, a path relative to the working directory, or an unqualified\n\
    \ path (without path separators) which will be resolved using the operating\n\
    \ system's equivalent of the PATH environment variable. Path separators\n\
