    \\STX\EOT/\DC2\ACK\206\DC2\NUL\218\DC2\SOH\SUB\150\n\
    \ Parameters for the FastCDC content-defined chunking algorithm.\n\
    \\n\
    \ Implementations MUST follow the FastCDC 2020 paper by Wen Xia, et al.:\n\
    \ https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9055082\n\
    \\n\
    \ Supported implementations:\n\
    \   - Rust: https://docs.rs/fastcdc/3.2.1/fastcdc/v2020/index.html\n\
    \   - Go: https://github.com/buildbuddy-io/fastcdc2020\n\
    \\n\
    \ Test vectors can be found in the accompanying fastcdc2020_test_vectors.txt file.\n\
    \\n\
    \ Implementations MUST use normalization level 2, which has been found\n\
    \ successful for build artifacts with an average chunk size of 512 KiB.\n\
    \\n\
    \ Key algorithm components from the paper:\n\
    \\n\
    \ GEAR table: 256 64-bit integers for the rolling hash, computed as:\n\
    \   GEAR[i] = high_64_bits(MD5(byte(i))) for i in 0..255\n\
    \\n\
    \ MASKS table: Bit patterns for chunk boundary detection, derived from\n\
    \ the C reference implementation. The mask selection based on average\n\
    \ chunk size SHOULD match the paper.\n\
    \\n\
    \ The minimum and maximum chunk sizes MUST be derived from the average:\n\
    \   - min_chunk_size = avg_chunk_size_bytes / 4\n\
    \   - max_chunk_size = avg_chunk_size_bytes * 4\n\
    \\n\
    \ Blobs smaller than max_chunk_size (avg_chunk_size_bytes * 4) SHOULD be\n\
    \ uploaded without chunking.\n\
    \\n\
    \ If any of the advertised parameters are not within the expected range,\n\
    \ the client SHOULD ignore FastCDC chunking function support.\n\
    \\n\
    \\v\n\
    \\ETX\EOT/\SOH\DC2\EOT\206\DC2\b\EM\n\
    \\174\SOH\n\
    \\EOT\EOT/\STX\NUL\DC2\EOT\210\DC2\STX\"\SUB\159\SOH The average (expected) chunk size for the FastCDC chunking algorithm.\n\
    \ The value MUST be between 1 KiB and 1 MiB. The recommended value is\n\
    \ 524288 (512 KiB).\n\
    \\n\
    \\r\n\
    \\ENQ\EOT/\STX\NUL\ENQ\DC2\EOT\210\DC2\STX\b\n\
    \\r\n\
    \\ENQ\EOT/\STX\NUL\SOH\DC2\EOT\210\DC2\t\GS\n\
    \\r\n\
    \\ENQ\EOT/\STX\NUL\ETX\DC2\EOT\210\DC2 !\n\
    \\168\SOH\n\
    \\EOT\EOT/\STX\SOH\DC2\EOT\217\DC2\STX\DC2\SUB\153\SOH The seed for the FastCDC mask generation.\n\
    \ The recommended value is 0.\n\
    \\n\
    \ All clients sharing a cache SHOULD use the same seed to maximize\n\
    \ chunk reuse.\n\
    \\n\
    \\r\n\
    \\ENQ\EOT/\STX\SOH\ENQ\DC2\EOT\217\DC2\STX\b\n\
    \\r\n\
    \\ENQ\EOT/\STX\SOH\SOH\DC2\EOT\217\DC2\t\r\n\
    \\r\n\
    \\ENQ\EOT/\STX\SOH\ETX\DC2\EOT\217\DC2\DLE\DC1\n\
    \\179\ENQ\n\
    \\STX\EOT0\DC2\ACK\237\DC2\NUL\249\DC2\SOH\SUB\164\ENQ Parameters for the RepMaxCDC content-defined chunking algorithm.\n\
    \\n\
    \ Supported implementations:\n\
    \   - Go: https://github.com/buildbarn/go-cdc\n\
    \\n\
    \ Key algorithm components:\n\
    \\n\
    \ GEAR table: 256 64-bit integers for the rolling hash, computed as:\n\
    \   GEAR[i] = high_64_bits(MD5(byte(i))) for i in 0..255\n\
    \\n\
    \ The algorithm repeatedly applies chunking until all chunks are in the\n\
    \ range [min_chunk_size_bytes, 2*min_chunk_size_bytes). Cutting points are\n\
    \ selected where the Gear rolling hash is maximized within a lookahead\n\
    \ window of horizon_size_bytes.\n\
    \\n\
    \ If any of the advertised parameters are not within the expected range,\n\
    \ the client SHOULD ignore RepMaxCDC chunking function support.\n\
    \\n\
    \\v\n\
    \\ETX\EOT0\SOH\DC2\EOT\237\DC2\b\ETB\n\
    \\140\STX\n\
    \\EOT\EOT0\STX\NUL\DC2\EOT\242\DC2\STX\"\SUB\253\SOH The minimum chunk size for the RepMaxCDC chunking algorithm.\n\
    \ The value MUST be at least 64 bytes (the Gear hash window size).\n\
    \ All chunks will be in the range [min_chunk_size_bytes, 2*min_chunk_size_bytes).\n\
    \ The recommended value is 262144 (256 KiB).\n\
    \\n\
    \\r\n\
    \\ENQ\EOT0\STX\NUL\ENQ\DC2\EOT\242\DC2\STX\b\n\
    \\r\n\
    \\ENQ\EOT0\STX\NUL\SOH\DC2\EOT\242\DC2\t\GS\n\
    \\r\n\
    \\ENQ\EOT0\STX\NUL\ETX\DC2\EOT\242\DC2 !\n\
    \\131\STX\n\
    \\EOT\EOT0\STX\SOH\DC2\EOT\248\DC2\STX \SUB\244\SOH The lookahead window for finding optimal cutting points.\n\
    \ Larger values improve deduplication quality with diminishing returns.\n\
    \ Setting to 0 produces uniform chunks of min_chunk_size_bytes.\n\
    \ The recommended value is 8 * min_chunk_size_bytes.\n\
    \\n\
    \\r\n\
    \\ENQ\EOT0\STX\SOH\ENQ\DC2\EOT\248\DC2\STX\b\n\
